    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "WHAT TO DO\n• IN AN EMERGENCY\n727200\nPSA\nPACIFIC SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\n2-4 2/79",
      "EXIT DOORS - Rotate han- RED loop to inflate evacua-\ndle in direction of arrow. tion slide. Remain standing\nPush door outward. Pull and jump into slide.\nSAFETY\nPRECAUTION\nRemove shoes\nand sharp objects\nfrom your person\nbefore using an\nevacuation slide.\nREAR CABIN DOOR\nThis exit may be\nused at the direc-\ntion of the flight\ncrew.\nOVERWING WINDOW EXIT",
      "AUTOMATIC OXYGEN\nSYSTEM - Should a loss of\ncabin pressure occur, oxy-\ngen masks will drop from\noverhead. Extinguishing\nall smoking materials, pull\nnearest mask down\nto\nstart the flow of oxygen.\nPlace mask over nose and\nmouth promptly, adjust\nheadband and breathe\nnormally.\nBRACING POSITIONS\nSeats\nfacing\nrearward\nSeats facing\nforward\nSEATBELTS\nKeep\nfastened\nwhile seated\n(TO RELEASE)\nFLOTATION EQUIPMENT - In the\nevent of a water landing, your\nseat cushion bottom should be us-\ned for flotation. Grasp the cushion\nat the rear, pull it forward and\ntake it with you. Place arms\nthrough straps on cushion bottom\nto retain.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE CARD FROM AIRCRAFT\n2002.127.449"
    ],
